      "name": {
        "name": "UDP-sugar pyrophosphorylase",
        "short": "UDP-sugar_pyrophosphorylase"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This entry includes UDP-sugar phosphorylases such as UDP-N-acetylglucosamine pyrophosphorylase, UDP-N-acetylhexosamine pyrophosphorylase (UAP1) and UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase, all of which catalyse the transfer of an uridylyl group.  UAP1 has two catalytic domains, UDP-N-acetylgalactosamine pyrophosphorylase ([ec:2.7.7.83]) and UDP-N-acetylglucosamine pyrophosphorylase ([ec:2.7.7.23]) [[cite:PUB00090041]].  UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase is required for the biosynthesis of UDP-glucosamine, an essential precursor for glycoprotein and glycolipid synthesis and can utilize UDP-glucosamine or UDP-galactosamine [[cite:PUB00090042]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
